  "tourWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to Kruftle",
  "tourWelcomeBody": "Build artifacts pile up quietly. Kruftle finds every project on your disk, works out what built it, and asks that toolchain to clean up after itself.",
  "tourWelcomeStart": "Show me around",
  "tourWelcomeSkip": "Skip the tour",
  "tourScanTitle": "Point it at a folder",
  "tourScanBody": "Choose your codebase root. Kruftle walks everything underneath, recognising more than forty languages and build tools from the files they leave behind — including projects nested inside other projects.",
  "tourReviewTitle": "See what it found before anything happens",
  "tourReviewBody": "Every project, every artifact directory, and what each one costs you — measured, not guessed. Tick what you want cleaned. Nothing is touched until you say so.",
  "tourSafetyTitle": "Safety is not optional",
  "tourSafetyBody": "Kruftle prefers each toolchain's own clean command over deleting files. Raw deletion is allow-listed by directory name, never follows a symlink, refuses to leave the folder you chose, and always asks first. Anything git tracks is left alone.",
  "tourCachesTitle": "The caches in your home directory too",
  "tourCachesBody": "Cargo's registry, Gradle's caches, the npm and pub caches — shared by every project and often the biggest win on the disk. They get their own screen and their own confirmation.",
  "tourScheduleTitle": "Set it and forget it",
  "tourScheduleBody": "Have Kruftle clean daily, weekly or monthly. It can nudge you while it is open, or register with your operating system's own scheduler and do the run with Kruftle closed.",
  "tourFinishTitle": "That's the whole app",
  "tourFinishBody": "Everything runs on your machine. Nothing is uploaded, and there is no account to make.",
  "tourFinishAction": "Get started",

